.TH STRING.HPP 3v32 "October 22, 2026" "v32c++ 20261022-dev" "v32c++ Library"
.SH NAME
v32/string.hpp \- v32::String, a fixed-capacity string over the Vircon32 SDK
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <v32/string.hpp>
.PP
.B namespace v32 {
.PP
.B class String {
.B "public:"
.B "    String();"
.BI "    String( int* " text " );"
.B "    int  length();"
.B "    int* c_str();"
.BI "    int  at( int " index " );"
.BI "    void assign( int* " text " );"
.BI "    void append( int* " text " );"
.BI "    void append_int( int " value ", int " base " );"
.BI "    void append_float( float " value " );"
.BI "    void operator+=( int* " text " );"
.BI "    void operator=( int* " text " );"
.BI "    bool equals( int* " text " );"
.BI "    bool operator==( int* " text " );"
.BI "    bool operator!=( int* " text " );"
.BI "    void print_at_xy( int " x ", int " y " );"
.B "    void print_current_point();"
.B };
.PP
.B }
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B v32::String
holds up to 127 characters in a 128-word array inside the object, so it
needs no heap and can be copied safely. It is built on the SDK's
.I string.h
and
.I video.h
(see
.BR string.h (3v32)),
which this header includes.
.PP
The built-in
.B std::string
(see
.BR v32c++\-string (3v32))
is an alternative with the standard C++ interface, which can also be
passed and returned by value.
.TP
.BR String() ", " String( text )
An empty string, or a copy of
.IR text .
.TP
.BR length ", " c_str
The length, and the characters as a plain zero-terminated
.B int*
for the SDK's functions.
.TP
.B at
The character at
.IR index ,
or 0 when
.I index
is out of range.
.TP
.BR assign ", " operator=
Replace the contents.
.TP
.BR append ", " operator+=
Append text.
.TP
.B append_int
Append a number in base 2 to 16, as
.BR itoa (3v32)
writes it.
.TP
.B append_float
Append a number with up to 5 decimals, as
.BR ftoa (3v32)
writes it (0.999999 is
.BR 1 ).
A value of 2147483648 or more, or below \-2147483648, which
.B ftoa
cannot format and hangs on, appends
.B overflow
or
.B \-overflow
instead.
.TP
.BR equals ", " operator== ", " operator!=
Compare with text.
.TP
.BR print_at_xy ", " print_current_point
Draw the string with the BIOS font, as
.BR print_at (3v32).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
#include <v32/string.hpp>

void show_score( int score )
{
    v32::String s( "SCORE " );
    s.append_int( score, 10 );
    s += " PTS";
    s.print_at_xy( 10, 10 );
}
.fi
.RE
.SH BUGS
Nothing checks the capacity: text that makes the string longer than
127 characters overruns the object.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR string.h (3v32),
.BR v32c++\-string (3v32),
.BR v32c++\-headers (3v32)
.SH AUTHOR
Matthew Haas
